-- title:
--   Primitives of E[p] via the special formal mathcal O_D-module
-- statement:
--   Let $q\neq q'$ be primes, let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ be such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`, i.e. $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ every nonzero element of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a unit exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order (an order — containing $1$, closed under multiplication, spanning the algebra over $\mathbb Q$, finitely generated — maximal among the orders containing it), let $\mu\in\Lambda$ satisfy $\mu^2=-(qq')\cdot 1$, and let $\mathrm{star}:\Lambda\to\Lambda$ satisfy $\mu\cdot\mathrm{star}(x)=\bar x\cdot\mu$. Let $N$ be a natural number, $p$ a prime, $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and $E$ a `FakeEllipticCurve` for $\Lambda,N$ over $k$ (a smooth proper scheme with connected two-dimensional fibres over $\operatorname{Spec}k$, carrying a commutative relative group law, a $\Lambda$-action compatible with the law and with the trace condition on tangent spaces, and the further data of the structure). Let $H$ be a finite commutative cocommutative Hopf $k$-algebra with $\dim_k H=p^{4}$ whose multiplication-by-$p$ endomorphism factors through the counit, and let $e$ be, for each $k$-algebra $T$, a bijection from $\mathrm{WithConv}(H\to_{\mathrm{alg}} T)$ onto the $p$-torsion of $E$ over $\operatorname{Spec}T$, compatible with the group laws on both sides and natural in $T$. Assume $p=q$ or $p=q'$. Then there exist a coordinate map $\mathrm{coord}:\Lambda\to \mathbb Z_{p^2}\times\mathbb Z_{p^2}$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (additive, sending $1$ to $(1,0)$, multiplicative for the twisted rule involving $p$ and the Witt Frobenius, injective, with dense image, and matching reduced traces), a ring homomorphism $j_0:\mathbb Z_{p^2}\to k$, a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ over $k$ relative to $j_0$ (a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $F$ with $\mathbb Z_{p^2}$-action and uniformiser $\varpi$ subject to the $\mathcal O_D$-relations, with complementary invertible Lie summands and of height $4$), and a $k$-linear map $\Psi$ from the primitives of $H$ (the kernel of $\Delta-x\otimes 1-1\otimes x$) to $k[[T_1,T_2]]$, such that, writing $I$ for the ideal generated by the components of the $p$-th iterate $[p]_F$ of $F$: each $\Psi(x)$ has zero constant term and its additive coboundary $F(\Psi x)-\Psi x(X)-\Psi x(Y)$ lies in the ideal of $k[[X,Y]]$ generated by the components of $[p]_F$ in the $X$-variables and in the $Y$-variables; $\Psi(x)\in I$ forces $x=0$; every series with zero constant term whose additive coboundary lies in that ideal is congruent to some $\Psi(x)$ modulo $I$; and for every $m\in\Lambda$ and every $k$-algebra endomorphism $\varphi_H$ of $H$ which corresponds under $e$, for all $T$, to composition with $E.\mathrm{act}\,m$ and which preserves the primitives, one has $\Psi(\varphi_H x)\equiv \Psi(x)\circ\bigl([\alpha]+_F[\beta]\circ\varpi\bigr) \pmod I$, where $(\alpha,\beta)=\mathrm{coord}(m)$.
--
--   This is the passage from the $p$-torsion Hopf algebra of a fake elliptic curve in a characteristic at which the quaternion algebra ramifies to the formal side: the primitives of $H$ are identified, modulo the $[p]$-ideal, with the additive $F$-cocycles of the special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module attached to $E$, compatibly with the $\Lambda$-action expressed through the coordinates $\mathrm{coord}$. It is used to compute the trace of the action of an element of $\Lambda$ on the primitives, in `trace_restrict_primitives_eq_intCast_of_charP_of_dvd`.
